    "body": "Quoting from the link you provided:\r\n\r\n> Cmd+K, on the other hand, is performed by Terminal itself, regardless of what's running in the window, so it might hide the output from the program.\r\n\r\nSo What terminal are you using? `cmd+k` inputs `[107;9u` and does nothing else on my Kitty terminal.\r\n\r\nI don't think this is a thing most programs, including Starship, should give special care. `cmd` a.k.a. `meta` key is never a standard for terminals.\r\n\r\nAlso, if you are looking for something like `line_sep` in Spaceship, there is similar config called  `add_newline` in Starship and it is enabled by default. Not sure if it works for you though.",
