    "body": "> Why should they? They are not the same thing and that's why they are different shortcuts.\r\n\r\nSorry, I mean I want a config to make `cmd+k` working same as `ctrl+l`, like https://github.com/spaceship-prompt/spaceship-prompt/issues/703\r\n\r\n> Also please don't just ignore my other questions. You still don't mention what terminal you are using, and cmd+k doesn't work in some terminals.\r\n\r\nI'm using zsh in VSCode.\r\n\r\n> if you prefer cmd+k because it's easier to reach, you should just rebind it to ctrl+l in your terminal or use something like Karabiner-Elements.\r\n\r\nI'm asking here because in `spaceship-prompt`, it works as expected to me with `line_sep` and no terminal configuration or key mapping.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nActually, I think the difference is that `spaceship-prompt` displays path with ending in a single line, but `starship` displays path with ending in two lines. So is there any config to make it possible?",
