    "updated_at": "2021-07-27T03:46:55Z",
    "body": "> Sorry, I mean I want a config to make `cmd+k` working same as `ctrl+l`, like [spaceship-prompt/spaceship-prompt#703](https://github.com/spaceship-prompt/spaceship-prompt/issues/703)\r\n\r\nThis is the last time I will repeat myself: they are different things and they will never work in the same way. What you are asking for is to make it *looks* like they are doing the same thing.\r\n\r\n> I'm using zsh in VSCode.\r\n\r\nOK, I can reproduce now.\r\n\r\n> Actually, I think the difference is that `spaceship-prompt` displays path with ending in a single line, but `starship` displays path with ending in two lines.\r\n\r\nYep, the \"Scrollback buffer\" being cleared with `cmd+k` includes the first line of the prompt, when using a two-line prompt. But if your prompt is only one line then it will be kept.\r\n\r\n> So is there any config to make it possible?\r\n\r\nhttps://starship.rs/config/#default-prompt-format\r\n\r\nRemove `$line_break\\` from the default config and you will get a single line prompt.\r\n",
